  "Question": "The sum of the numerical coefficients of all the terms in the expansion of \\((x-2y)^{18}\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0\\)",
    "B": "\\(1\\)",
    "C": "\\(19\\)",
    "D": "\\(-1\\)",
    "E": "\\(-19\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "When \\(x=y=1\\), every variable factor in an expanded term becomes \\(1\\), so each term becomes its signed numerical coefficient. Therefore evaluating the original expression at these values gives the coefficient sum:\n\\[\n(1-2)^{18}=(-1)^{18}=1.\n\\]\nThe sum is \\(\\boxed{1}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
